    {
      "id": "claim_7e49a3b0e00a46e88fe8a937f019eeda",
      "statement": "`deploy/daily.sh` uses strict shell failure handling, restores the S3 `store/` working copy, runs sync then status then per-asset binning, and performs the normal store, dated-run, and image-digest S3 writes only after those stage gates succeed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://deploy/daily.sh#L14-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:88fc633667d0300731bdd84472dc424e1f9c64175ea2badb666472d91aeb4efc:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://deploy/daily.sh#L70-L180",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:42f8b92b4e3d3f951b36bea0c0ac2cdb500ec9805522d5f74324c9e6b3dfb5bc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d81135a4f40b496893b7dcc40fe07d8f",
      "statement": "The final store sync, run-artifact sync, and digest upload are sequential AWS commands rather than a transaction, so a failure during final publication stops later commands but cannot roll back an earlier successful upload.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://deploy/daily.sh#L172-L181",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:068c756f614db73f0f4ac137a700784b5956deda078c87b484319a7c2ebcd450:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7a5b12cb659b40e482389c279d530e99",
      "statement": "The script captures `JEF_IMAGE_DIGEST` once from caller input or ECS v4 task metadata, optionally derives task CPU and memory inputs from that same metadata, creates and exports one UTC `JEF_RUN_STAMP`, and writes the digest beside a green run's artifacts.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://deploy/daily.sh#L16-L54",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:44ffedf414557586605b420a622337d404a4d48e2e50cb4409e36efc4bc2f96d:"
